                        "glosses": [
                            "A river that forms the boundary between Ceredigion and Carmarthenshire; the Teifi."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f351f361-4429-4774-a365-d4a948299f97",
                                "sense_id": "787f3535-f00c-30bb-8ff6-2bd9444c1a42",
                                "text": "With Cardigan the Muſe proceeds,\nAnd tells what rare things Tivy breeds:\nNext, proud Plynillimon ſhe plys;\nWhere Severn, Wy and Rydoll riſe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "83b96d11-52e4-4f70-93dd-6ebe4b2c08f5",
                                "sense_id": "787f3535-f00c-30bb-8ff6-2bd9444c1a42",
                                "text": "1688, Edmund Bohun, Caermarthenſhire, entry in A Geographical Dictionary, unnumbered page,\nIt takes its name from the principal City, which ſtands upon the River Tivy, about five Miles from the Sea."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d1c9527-4089-438e-8353-096d29b1efc5",
                                "sense_id": "787f3535-f00c-30bb-8ff6-2bd9444c1a42",
                                "text": "From thence we first gained a view of the vale through which the Tivy runs, intersecting a broad plain with its manifold windings, and crossed in the centre by a narrow bridge of one arch, just below the town of Llanbeder."
                            }
